From: Qianzf <qianzf@example.com>
Subject: [PATCH] qca-ssdk: declare the mdio i2c bus data locally

The SFP i2c path refers to struct qcom_mdio_i2c_data which only the
QSDK mdio-ipq4019 driver exports.  Declare the single member it uses;
the path is dormant on boards without an SFP cage.

Signed-off-by: Qianzf <qianzf@example.com>
---
--- a/src/hsl/phy/sfp_phy.c	2026-07-20 11:22:55.000000000 +0800
+++ b/src/hsl/phy/sfp_phy.c	2026-11-21 10:47:04.860631587 +0800
@@ -28,6 +28,15 @@
 #include <linux/phylink.h>
 #include <linux/sfp.h>
 
+/*
+ * The QSDK mdio-ipq4019 driver exports this struct for the SFP i2c path.
+ * Mainline keeps the structure private, so declare the one member used
+ * here; this board has no SFP cage and the path stays dormant.
+ */
+struct qcom_mdio_i2c_data {
+	struct i2c_adapter *i2c;
+};
+
 static a_bool_t sfp_phy_drv_registered = A_FALSE;
 
 static int sfp_eeprom_i2c_read(struct phy_device *phydev, u32 bus_addr,
